IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je21-nouns`
IMPORT `je21-seat-defaults`
IMPORT `je21-art01-definitions`
IMPORT `je21-art02-making`
IMPORT `je21-art03-commencement`
IMPORT `je21-art26-commencement`

-- je21-seat-1-making-and-commencement: the questions a reader of an enactment asks about what an instrument is, how it is made and when it starts.
-- The seat is the reader of an enactment, and each exported name is a question in that reader's words.
-- Each question takes the facts the reader can state and no reading of a fork: it uses the default in je21-seat-defaults.
-- Where the Law has two deposited texts and the answer can turn on which governs, the question is asked as at a day, and a day before the Law was in force is answered with a value that says so, not a refusal.
-- A rule module's FALSE for "permits" means the Article does not give the effect; where the Law is silent about the rest, the exported question refuses and says so.
-- A question whether an Article applies, requires or bars is answered by the Article's own words (NOTES.md section 2), and on the separate applicability clauses by the reading of fork L12.

§ `The Law itself`

-- src:223 | This Law may be cited as the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 and comes into force on a day to be specified by the States by Act.
-- src:258 | (Jersey) Law 2021
-- src:259 | L.8/2021
-- src:260 | 28
-- src:261 | September 2021 (R&O.112/2021)
-- src:268 | [2] Article 2(1) revised
-- src:269 | on 11 January 2024 by Law Revision Board item 2023/1
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 26 and the endnotes (src:223, src:258-261, src:268-269)
@export Which text of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 governs on a given day? The answer is that the Law was not in force, the text in force from 28 September 2021, or the text in force from 11 January 2024.
GIVEN day IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about
GIVETH A `Text of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021`
`Which text of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 governs on a given day?` day MEANS
    `Article 26 and the endnotes: which text of the Law governs on the day` day

-- src:223 | This Law may be cited as the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 and comes into force on a day to be specified by the States by Act.
-- src:258 | (Jersey) Law 2021
-- src:259 | L.8/2021
-- src:260 | 28
-- src:261 | September 2021 (R&O.112/2021)
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 26 and the endnotes (src:223, src:258-261)
@export Was the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 in force at some time on a given day?
GIVEN day IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Was the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 in force at some time on a given day?` day MEANS
    `Article 26: the Law was in force at some time on the day` day

§ `What an instrument is`

-- src:11 | “Jersey legislation” means any Law or Jersey subordinate legislation;
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 1 "Jersey legislation" (src:11)
@export Is this instrument Jersey legislation? Jersey legislation is any Law or Jersey subordinate legislation.
GIVEN instrument IS A `Facts about an instrument` @desc The facts about the instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is this instrument Jersey legislation?` instrument MEANS
    `Article 1 "Jersey legislation": the instrument is Jersey legislation` instrument FALSE

-- src:15 | “Law” means Jersey legislation adopted by the States that does not rely on any other legislation to empower its making;
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 1 "Law" (src:15)
@export Is this instrument a Law, that is Jersey legislation adopted by the States that does not rely on any other legislation to empower its making?
GIVEN instrument IS A `Facts about an instrument` @desc The facts about the instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is this instrument a Law?` instrument MEANS
    `Article 1 "Law": the instrument is a Law` instrument FALSE

-- src:12 | “Jersey subordinate legislation” means any Regulations, Order or other instrument having legislative effect in Jersey that is made in Jersey under –
-- src:13 | (a) any Jersey legislation; or
-- src:14 | (b) any UK extended legislation or Order in Council registered in the Royal Court;
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 1 "Jersey subordinate legislation" (src:12-14)
@export Is this instrument Jersey subordinate legislation, that is Regulations, an Order or another instrument having legislative effect in Jersey that is made in Jersey under Jersey legislation, UK extended legislation or an Order in Council registered in the Royal Court?
GIVEN instrument IS A `Facts about an instrument` @desc The facts about the instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is this instrument Jersey subordinate legislation?` instrument MEANS
    `Article 1 "Jersey subordinate legislation": the instrument is Jersey subordinate legislation` instrument FALSE

-- src:28 | “UK extended legislation” means any provision of a UK Act, or subordinate legislation made under a UK Act, that has been registered in the Royal Court.[1]
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 1 "UK extended legislation" (src:28)
@export Is this instrument UK extended legislation, that is a provision of a UK Act, or subordinate legislation made under a UK Act, that has been registered in the Royal Court?
GIVEN instrument IS A `Facts about an instrument` @desc The facts about the instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is this instrument UK extended legislation?` instrument MEANS
    `Article 1 "UK extended legislation": the instrument is UK extended legislation` instrument FALSE

§ `How Jersey legislation is made`

-- src:32 | (1) A Law is made –
-- src:33 | (a) by being adopted by the States Assembly;
-- src:34 | (b) by being sanctioned by Order in Council; and
-- src:35 | (c) by being registered in the Royal Court.[2]
-- src:36 | (2) A taxation draft declared by Act of the States to have effect under Article 12(1) of the Public Finances (Jersey) Law 2019 is to be treated as having been made as a Law even though it has not yet completed the steps referred to in paragraph (1)(b) and (c).
-- src:42 | (4) Subject to paragraph (2), Jersey legislation has been made once it has been registered, adopted or signed as the case may be.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 2(1), (2) and (4) (src:32-36, src:42)
@export Has this Law been made, as at a given day? A Law is made by being adopted by the States Assembly, sanctioned by Order in Council and registered in the Royal Court. A taxation draft declared by Act of the States is treated as made.
GIVEN day IS A DATE @desc The day as at which you are asking, which decides which text of the Law governs
      steps IS A `Steps toward making a Law` @desc The steps taken so far toward making the Law
GIVETH AN EITHER `Before the Law was in force` BOOLEAN
`Has this Law been made?` day steps MEANS
    CONSIDER `Article 26 and the endnotes: which text of the Law governs on the day` day
    WHEN `the Law was not in force`
        THEN LEFT (`the Law was not in force on that date` `Article 26: the commencement of the Law, as the endnotes record it`)
    WHEN `the text of 28 September 2021`
        THEN RIGHT (`Article 2 (text of 28 September 2021): the Law has been made` steps `default reading L8`)
    WHEN `the text of 11 January 2024`
        THEN RIGHT (`Article 2 (text of 11 January 2024): the Law has been made` steps `default reading L8`)

-- src:32 | (1) A Law is made –
-- src:33 | (a) by being adopted by the States Assembly;
-- src:34 | (b) by being sanctioned by Order in Council; and
-- src:35 | (c) by being registered in the Royal Court.[2]
-- src:36 | (2) A taxation draft declared by Act of the States to have effect under Article 12(1) of the Public Finances (Jersey) Law 2019 is to be treated as having been made as a Law even though it has not yet completed the steps referred to in paragraph (1)(b) and (c).
-- src:42 | (4) Subject to paragraph (2), Jersey legislation has been made once it has been registered, adopted or signed as the case may be.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 2(1), (2) and (4) (src:32-36, src:42)
@export On what day was this Law made, as at a given day? Once the Law has been made, it is made on the day it was registered; the answer is empty if it has not been made.
GIVEN day IS A DATE @desc The day as at which you are asking, which decides whether the Law was in force
      steps IS A `Steps toward making a Law` @desc The steps taken so far toward making the Law
GIVETH AN EITHER `Before the Law was in force` (MAYBE DATE)
`On what day was this Law made?` day steps MEANS
    IF `Article 26: the Law was in force at some time on the day` day
    THEN RIGHT (`Article 2(4): the day on which the Law was made` steps `default reading L4` `default reading L8`)
    ELSE LEFT (`the Law was not in force on that date` `Article 26: the commencement of the Law, as the endnotes record it`)

-- src:37 | (3) Jersey subordinate legislation is made –
-- src:38 | (a) in the case of Regulations (including Triennial Regulations) or an Act that is Jersey legislation, by the proposition containing the Regulations or Act being adopted by the States Assembly; or
-- src:39 | (b) in the case of any other Jersey subordinate legislation, by being signed by –
-- src:40 | (i) the person responsible for making it, or
-- src:41 | (ii) if made by a body, a person acting in accordance with any procedural requirements of the body.
-- src:42 | (4) Subject to paragraph (2), Jersey legislation has been made once it has been registered, adopted or signed as the case may be.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 2(3) and (4) (src:37-42)
@export Has this subordinate legislation been made, as at a given day? Regulations and Acts are made when the States Assembly adopts the proposition containing them; other subordinate legislation when it is signed by the person responsible or, for a body, by a person acting in accordance with its procedure.
GIVEN day IS A DATE @desc The day as at which you are asking, which decides whether the Law was in force
      steps IS A `Steps toward making subordinate legislation` @desc The steps taken so far toward making the subordinate legislation
GIVETH AN EITHER `Before the Law was in force` BOOLEAN
`Has this subordinate legislation been made?` day steps MEANS
    IF `Article 26: the Law was in force at some time on the day` day
    THEN RIGHT (`Article 2(3): the subordinate legislation has been adopted or signed as the Law requires` steps)
    ELSE LEFT (`the Law was not in force on that date` `Article 26: the commencement of the Law, as the endnotes record it`)

-- src:37 | (3) Jersey subordinate legislation is made –
-- src:38 | (a) in the case of Regulations (including Triennial Regulations) or an Act that is Jersey legislation, by the proposition containing the Regulations or Act being adopted by the States Assembly; or
-- src:39 | (b) in the case of any other Jersey subordinate legislation, by being signed by –
-- src:40 | (i) the person responsible for making it, or
-- src:41 | (ii) if made by a body, a person acting in accordance with any procedural requirements of the body.
-- src:42 | (4) Subject to paragraph (2), Jersey legislation has been made once it has been registered, adopted or signed as the case may be.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 2(3) and (4) (src:37-42)
@export On what day was this subordinate legislation made, as at a given day? The answer is empty if it has not been made.
GIVEN day IS A DATE @desc The day as at which you are asking, which decides whether the Law was in force
      steps IS A `Steps toward making subordinate legislation` @desc The steps taken so far toward making the subordinate legislation
GIVETH AN EITHER `Before the Law was in force` (MAYBE DATE)
`On what day was this subordinate legislation made?` day steps MEANS
    IF `Article 26: the Law was in force at some time on the day` day
    THEN RIGHT (`Article 2(4): the day on which the subordinate legislation was made` steps)
    ELSE LEFT (`the Law was not in force on that date` `Article 26: the commencement of the Law, as the endnotes record it`)

§ `When Jersey legislation starts`

-- src:45 | (1) If Jersey legislation is silent as to the commencement of any of its provisions that provision comes into force –
-- src:46 | (a) in the case of legislation having effect only to commence other legislation or consisting of an Act of the States referred to in Article 2(2), when it is made; and
-- src:47 | (b) in the case of any other legislation, on the day after it is made.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3(1) (src:45-47)
@export On what day does a provision that says nothing about when it starts come into force? Legislation that only commences other legislation, and an Act of the States referred to in Article 2(2), start when made; any other legislation starts on the day after it is made. The Law was in force from 28 September 2021, and a provision made earlier is answered with a value that says so.
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of legislation for Article 3(1)` @desc What kind of legislation the provision is part of
      `the day on which the legislation was made` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the legislation was made
GIVETH AN EITHER `Before the Law was in force` DATE
`On what day does a provision that says nothing about when it starts come into force?` kind `the day on which the legislation was made` MEANS
    IF `Article 26: the Law was in force at some time on the day` `the day on which the legislation was made`
    THEN RIGHT (`the day of a moment` (`Article 3(1): the moment a provision that is silent as to its commencement comes into force` kind `the day on which the legislation was made` NOTHING `default reading L1`))
    ELSE LEFT (`the Law was not in force on that date` `Article 26: the commencement of the Law, as the endnotes record it`)

-- src:45 | (1) If Jersey legislation is silent as to the commencement of any of its provisions that provision comes into force –
-- src:46 | (a) in the case of legislation having effect only to commence other legislation or consisting of an Act of the States referred to in Article 2(2), when it is made; and
-- src:47 | (b) in the case of any other legislation, on the day after it is made.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3(1) (src:45-47)
@export Was a provision that says nothing about when it starts in force at a given time of day on a given day? The Law says the provision starts on the day after it is made, and does not say at what time of that day, so a question about a time of day on that day is refused.
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of legislation for Article 3(1)` @desc What kind of legislation the provision is part of
      `the day on which the legislation was made` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the legislation was made
      `the time of day at which it was made, if known` IS A MAYBE `Time of day` @desc The time of day at which the legislation was made, in Jersey time; leave empty if not known
      `the day you are asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about
      `the time of day you are asking about` IS A `Time of day` @desc The time of day you are asking about, in Jersey time
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Was a provision that says nothing about when it starts in force at a given time of day?` kind `the day on which the legislation was made` `the time of day at which it was made, if known` `the day you are asking about` `the time of day you are asking about` MEANS
    `Article 3: the provision was in force at a time of day on the day`
        (`Article 3(1): the moment a provision that is silent as to its commencement comes into force` kind `the day on which the legislation was made` `the time of day at which it was made, if known` `default reading L1`)
        `the day you are asking about`
        `the time of day you are asking about`

-- src:54 | (6) Nothing in this Article affects the commencement of any Jersey legislation that had commenced before the commencement of this Part.
-- src:258 | (Jersey) Law 2021
-- src:259 | L.8/2021
-- src:260 | 28
-- src:261 | September 2021 (R&O.112/2021)
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3(6) and the endnotes (src:54, src:258-261)
@export Does Article 3 govern when this legislation started? It does not for legislation that had started before Part 2 of the Law came into force on 28 September 2021.
GIVEN `the day on which the legislation started, if it has` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The day on which the legislation started, under whatever rule applied; leave empty if it has not started
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does Article 3 govern when this legislation started?` `the day on which the legislation started, if it has` MEANS
    `Article 3(6): Article 3 governs when the legislation commenced` `the day on which the legislation started, if it has` `default reading L3`

-- src:49 | (3) Unless provision is made to the contrary, Regulations may provide that they commence by an Order of a Minister.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3(3) (src:49)
@export Can these Regulations provide that they start by an Order of a Minister? Regulations can, unless provision is made to the contrary.
GIVEN `the instrument is Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the instrument is Regulations
      `provision is made to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the empowering legislation or the Regulations themselves make provision to the contrary
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can these Regulations provide that they start by an Order of a Minister?` `the instrument is Regulations` `provision is made to the contrary` MEANS
    IF `Article 3(3): Regulations may provide that they commence by an Order of a Minister` `the instrument is Regulations` `provision is made to the contrary`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE REFUSE "Article 3(3) lets Regulations provide this unless provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say whether any other instrument can, or what follows where provision is made to the contrary"

-- src:50 | (4) If a Law, Regulations made under a Law or any provision of a Law or Regulations may be commenced by an Act of the States or an Order of a Minister on a day specified in the Act or Order, the power may be exercised to specify different days, times or events for different provisions of the Law or Regulations to commence.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3(4) (src:50)
@export Can a power to start a Law or Regulations by Act or Order name different days, times or events for different provisions?
GIVEN `it is a Law, Regulations made under a Law, or a provision of either` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the thing to be started is a Law, Regulations made under a Law, or a provision of either
      `it may be commenced by an Act of the States or an Order of a Minister on a day specified in the Act or Order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the Act or Order may bring it into force on a day it specifies
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can a commencement power name different days, times or events for different provisions?` `it is a Law, Regulations made under a Law, or a provision of either` `it may be commenced by an Act of the States or an Order of a Minister on a day specified in the Act or Order` MEANS
    IF `Article 3(4): the power may specify different days, times or events for different provisions` `it is a Law, Regulations made under a Law, or a provision of either` `it may be commenced by an Act of the States or an Order of a Minister on a day specified in the Act or Order` `default reading L12`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE REFUSE "Article 3(4) speaks of a Law, Regulations made under a Law or a provision of either that may be commenced by Act or Order on a specified day, and the Law does not say whether any other power can name different days, times or events"

-- src:51 | (5) If any Jersey legislation amends any other legislation or provision that has not come into force –
-- src:52 | (a) the amendment of the uncommenced legislation does not commence that legislation or provision; and
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3(5)(a) (src:51-52)
@export Does amending legislation that has not yet come into force bring that legislation into force? It does not.
GIVEN `the legislation or provision amended has not come into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the legislation or provision amended has not come into force
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does an amendment of uncommenced legislation commence it?` `the legislation or provision amended has not come into force` MEANS
    `Article 3(5)(a): the amendment of uncommenced legislation commences the legislation amended` `the legislation or provision amended has not come into force`

-- src:53 | (b) the amendment made by the amending legislation commences when the provision amended commences unless provision is made otherwise.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3(5)(b) (src:53)
@export On what day does an amendment of legislation that has not yet come into force start? It starts when the provision amended starts, unless provision is made otherwise. The answer is empty if neither day is known.
GIVEN `the day on which the provision amended comes into force, if it has` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The day on which the provision amended comes into force; leave empty if it has not
      `provision is made otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if provision is made that the amendment starts at some other time
      `the day that other provision gives, if any` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The day that other provision gives; leave empty if none
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`On what day does an amendment of uncommenced legislation start?` `the day on which the provision amended comes into force, if it has` `provision is made otherwise` `the day that other provision gives, if any` MEANS
    `the day of a moment, if any`
        (`Article 3(5)(b): the moment at which the amendment commences`
            (`the moment of a day, if any` `the day on which the provision amended comes into force, if it has`)
            `provision is made otherwise`
            (`the moment of a day, if any` `the day that other provision gives, if any`))

§ `Helpers`

-- The day a moment falls on.
GIVEN moment IS A `Moment of coming into force`
GIVETH A DATE
`the day of a moment` moment MEANS
    CONSIDER moment
    WHEN `from the beginning of the day` first THEN first
    WHEN `from a stated time on the day` first stated THEN first
    WHEN `from the time it was made on the day` first made THEN first
    WHEN `at a time on the day that the Law does not state` first THEN first

-- The day a moment falls on, if there is a moment.
GIVEN moment IS A MAYBE `Moment of coming into force`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day of a moment, if any` moment MEANS
    CONSIDER moment
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST m THEN JUST (`the day of a moment` m)

-- The moment a day begins, if there is a day.
GIVEN day IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `Moment of coming into force`
`the moment of a day, if any` day MEANS
    CONSIDER day
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST d THEN JUST (`from the beginning of the day` d)
